novaeng.extendable_storage_subsystem.info.0=The §acore§7 of the §9Storage Subsystem§7.
novaeng.extendable_storage_subsystem.info.1=Max Length: §a12
novaeng.extendable_fabricator_subsystem.info.0=The §acore§7 of the §eFabricator Subsystem§7.
novaeng.extendable_fabricator_subsystem.info.1=Max Length: §a12
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.0=The §acore§7 of the §bCalculator Subsystem§7.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.1=Max Length: §a12
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.2=The Calculator Subsystem introduces the concept of §bVirtual Crafting Processors§7 (abbreviated as §bvCPUs§7), accessible via the ME Communication Interface.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.3=§bVirtual Crafting Processor (vCPU)§7:
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.4=  The Mainframe initially provides only one §bvCPU§7 to the ME network, with a capacity equal to all currently available bytes in the subsystem.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.5=  When user submits a crafting task to a §bvCPU§7, the Mainframe automatically adjusts the vCPU's byte count to match the task's requirement and assigns it to a §bThread Core§7.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.6=  After assignment, if the current available bytes in the system are greater than §e10%%§7, a new §bvCPU§7 is automatically allocated; otherwise, allocation §cstops§7 until available bytes exceed §e10%%§7.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.7=  New §bvCPUs§7 can be allocated as long as the number of assigned vCPUs does not exceed the §eMax Thread Count§7.
novaeng.extendable_calculate_subsystem.info.8=  The §bvCPU§7 is §aimmediately deallocate§7 after the crafting task completes and §eall items are returned§7.

novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.info.0=§5Parallel Core§7 provides §5Parallelism§7 for the Fabricator Subsystem.
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.info.1=§5Parallelism§7 increases the §aprocessing amount§7 per crafting task for §bWorker Cores§7 (up to the queue depth).
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.modifiers=§5Parallelism§7 Modifiers:
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.overclock_modifiers=When §cOverclock§7 enabled:
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.modifier.add=Max Parallelism: §a+%s
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.modifier.sub=Max Parallelism Modifier: §c-%s
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.modifier.mul=Max Parallelism Modifier: §a+%s%%
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.modifier.mul.debuff=Max Parallelism Modifier: §c-%s%%
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.info.2=When §9Active Cooling§7 enabled:
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.info.3=  §aRemoves§7 the §cnegative§7 modifiers from overclocking.
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.info.4=  Overflow parallelism beyond the maximum is converted into a §areduction§7 in work interval and consumes §9Coolant§7, with a minimum of §b1§7 Tick (§b0.05s§7).
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.info.5=    For every §e5%%§7 overflow of max parallelism, the subsystem's work interval is reduced by §b1§7 Tick (§b0.05s§7).
novaeng.efabricator_parallel_proc.info.6=    For every §b1§7 Tick (§b0.05s§7) reduction in work interval, an additional §cMax Parallelism * 4%%§7 cooling units are consumed.

novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.0=§bWorker Core§7 is the §emain part§7 of the Fabricator Subsystem.
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.1=Each core has a queue depth of §a32§7 and processes §a1§7 crafting task per operation.
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.2=Energy consumption per craft: §b100 AE
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.3=When §cOverclock§7 enabled:
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.4=  Queue Depth §ax2 §b(F4)
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.5=  Queue Depth §ax4 §6(F6)
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.6=  Queue Depth §ax8 §5(F9)
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.7=  Energy Consumption §cx4 §b(F4)
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.8=  Energy Consumption §cx8 §6(F6)
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.9=  Energy Consumption §cx16 §5(F9)
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.10=When §9Active Cooling§7 enabled:
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.11=  §aRemoves§7 the §cnegative§7 modifiers from overclocking.
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.12=  Consumes an additional §c5§7 cooling units per craft.
novaeng.efabricator_worker.info.13=  Each Worker Core reduces the subsystem's work interval by §b1§7 Tick (§b0.05s§7), with a minimum of §b10§7 Ticks (§b0.5s§7).

novaeng.efabricator_pattern_bus.info.0=§ePattern Bus§7 is the §emain part§7 of the Fabricator Subsystem.
novaeng.efabricator_pattern_bus.info.1=The §ePattern Bus§7 stores §bPatterns§7 for the subsystem, each bus has §a72§7 pattern slots.
novaeng.efabricator_pattern_bus.info.2=Compatible with §bCrafting Patterns§7 / §aFluid Assembler Patterns§7, §cnot compatible with other patterns§7 (e.g., Processing Patterns).
novaeng.efabricator_pattern_bus.info.3=You can use §bQuick Upload§7 when encoding §eCrafting Patterns§7 in the ME Pattern Terminal.
novaeng.efabricator_pattern_bus.info.4=  There §cmust§7 be at least §aone online§7 subsystem in the network.
novaeng.efabricator_pattern_bus.info.5=  There §cmust§7 be at least §b1§7 §ePattern Bus§7 with an available pattern slot in the subsystem.

novaeng.efabricator_me_channel.info.0=§9Matrix Communication Interface§7 is the §bprotocol compatibility layer§7 between the subsystem and the ME network.
novaeng.efabricator_me_channel.info.1=  The §9Communication Interface§7 provides the ME network with access to the Pattern Core.
novaeng.efabricator_me_channel.info.2=  The subsystem can only receive power through the §9Communication Interface§7.
novaeng.efabricator_me_channel.info.3=Connect ME Cable to the §9Communication Interface§7 to establish a connection between the ME network and the subsystem.

